cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "apiary: a local multi-agent coding swarm"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shahrestani
    given-names: Kamyar
    email: info@shahrestani.me
    alias: kamyarshahrestani
repository-code: "https://github.com/shahrestani-me/apiary"
abstract: >-
  A fully local multi-agent coding system for Apple Silicon. A LangGraph
  orchestrator decomposes an objective into non-overlapping tasks, runs each in
  an isolated git worktree with an Ollama-hosted model, and admits results only
  when a real verification command exits zero. Explores whether verification and
  filesystem isolation, rather than agent-level reasoning about coordination, are
  what make multi-agent code generation reliable at small model scales.
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - large language models
  - local-first
  - code generation
  - program verification
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
